      "facts": [
        "While paused, when the paused hour stops waiting.",
        "A paused hour (`freebuff-session-pause.ts`): the time the next session on this model resumes it with. Absent on a running hour.",
        "Pausing a paid hour (2026-11-24, product): a running session can stop its clock and keep the time it has left for later, less a fixed cost. The cost is the prompt cache: a paused chat's cached context is gone when it comes back, so its first turns are billed at the full input price.",
        "Only an hour a hosted chat (Web, Desktop's workspace window) or a current CLI holds can pause: those are the purchases in `freebuff_desktop_purchase`. The server decides (`pauseDesktopPurchase`); clients use these figures to say beforehand what a pause would keep.",
        "What pausing takes off the time left.",
        "The least a pause may keep: below this there is nothing worth saving."
      ],
